                <pb facs="0811" n="715" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg715"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861a.01/67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-31T18:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">August 31,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 31—4:29
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Petroff, Chairman Council of Ministers Far Eastern Republic, and Kraajew Nikoff
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">Kozhevnikov</hi>], Assistant Secretary of State,
                    arrived in Harbin yesterday from Chita <hi rendition="#italic">en route</hi> to
                    Dairen where they expect to confer with Japanese. Party had some difficulty with
                    maritime customs but matter finally arranged and they expect continue journey
                    today. Legation informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
